# motoquencer `constantlength = 1`, the search rule. motoquencer.md:922 — "the
# repeats in step 4 are reduced by 1. If they are already 1, step 5 is tried an so
# on, until it wrap around to step 1."
#
# So the hunt for slack runs FORWARD from the edited step, wraps round the end of
# the range, and steps over any step already at the floor of 1 repeat.
#
# Step 3 holds 5 repeats; steps 1, 2 and 4 hold 1. Step 4 is dialled up by 2: the
# search wraps to step 1 (at the floor, nothing to give), tries step 2 (likewise)
# and lands on step 3, which gives up its 2 (5 -> 3). The cycle stays 8 clocks.
#
# The second half shows the other direction: dialling step 4 back DOWN by 2 hands
# the 2 to the first step the forward search meets — step 1, now 3 repeats. The
# compensation is a fresh greedy search each time, not an undo stack, so the
# sequence does not fold back to where it started; only its length does.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock          = I1
    fadermode      = I2
    constantlength = I3
    numsteps       = 4
    numfaders      = 4
    quantize       = 0
    cvbase         = 0
    cvrange        = 1
    defaultgate    = 1
    cv             = O1
>>>
@2 move F1 0.0
@3 move F2 0.25
@4 move F3 0.5
@5 move F4 0.75
@6 set I2 3
# with the feature off, give step 3 five repeats (notch 4)
@7 move F3 0.2666667
@7 expect F3 0.2666667 tol 1e-4
@8 set I3 1
# step 4: 1 -> 3 repeats. Steps 1 and 2 are at the floor; step 3 pays (5 -> 3).
@9 move F4 0.1333333
@9 expect F4 0.1333333 tol 1e-4
@9 expect F1 0 tol 1e-4
@9 expect F2 0 tol 1e-4
@9 expect F3 0.1333333 tol 1e-4
# step 4: 3 -> 1 repeats. The 2 clocks have to go somewhere: step 1 takes them.
@10 move F4 0.0
@10 expect F4 0 tol 1e-4
@10 expect F1 0.1333333 tol 1e-4
@10 expect F2 0 tol 1e-4
@10 expect F3 0.1333333 tol 1e-4
@11 set I2 0
# still 8 clocks: step 1 three times, step 2 once, step 3 three times, step 4 once.
@13 set I1 1
@13 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@14 set I1 0
@15 set I1 1
@15 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@16 set I1 0
@17 set I1 1
@17 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@18 set I1 0
@19 set I1 1
@19 expect O1 0.25 tol 1e-4
@20 set I1 0
@21 set I1 1
@21 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@22 set I1 0
@23 set I1 1
@23 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@24 set I1 0
@25 set I1 1
@25 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@26 set I1 0
@27 set I1 1
@27 expect O1 0.75 tol 1e-4
@28 set I1 0
@29 set I1 1
@29 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@30 set I1 0
